WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:05.720
So what do we mean with no join?

00:05.720 --> 00:10.160
Well, we want the returns, the data from two tables without combining them.

00:10.160 --> 00:14.080
So actually this is not a join type because we are not combining anything.

00:14.080 --> 00:16.520
We just want to query the data from two tables.

00:16.520 --> 00:20.800
So that means from the table A we want to see all the rows everything.

00:20.800 --> 00:24.480
And from the table B we want to see everything as well all the rows.

00:24.480 --> 00:28.320
So that means we want to see two results and there is no need to combine them.

00:28.320 --> 00:30.040
So let's see the syntax of that.

00:30.040 --> 00:31.800
So what we have to do is very simple.

00:31.800 --> 00:35.000
Select star from table A and then semicolon.

00:35.000 --> 00:36.840
And then start another query.

00:36.880 --> 00:38.400
Select star from table B.

00:38.400 --> 00:39.320
So that's it.

00:39.320 --> 00:43.760
And of course since we are not combining the data there will be no join in the syntax.

00:43.760 --> 00:44.560
So that's it.

00:44.560 --> 00:46.640
Let's go to SQL in order to do that okay.

00:46.680 --> 00:47.920
So now we have the following task.

00:47.920 --> 00:53.200
It says retrieve all data from customers and orders in two different results.

00:53.200 --> 00:56.480
So that sounds that we don't have to go and combine the tables together.

00:56.520 --> 00:56.880
And all.

00:56.880 --> 00:58.160
What you can do is the following.

00:58.200 --> 01:02.400
We can go and select the data from the first table like this.

01:02.400 --> 01:07.640
And then we make another query for the second table the orders.

01:07.640 --> 01:10.680
And we don't have to go and combine them in one big query.

01:10.720 --> 01:14.400
We just use a very simple Select statements in order to retrieve the data.

01:14.400 --> 01:18.960
So if you go and execute it, since you have two separate queries, you will get two results.

01:18.960 --> 01:23.600
And with that in one result you will get all the customers and in the other result you will get all

01:23.600 --> 01:26.960
the orders and the data is not combined at all.

01:26.960 --> 01:30.280
So this is how you query two tables without combining them.

01:30.280 --> 01:33.240
So with that you are getting all the data without joining the tables.

01:33.280 --> 01:38.320
Now we're going to start talking about the first type of join the inner join where we start combining

01:38.320 --> 01:39.640
the data from two tables.

01:39.640 --> 01:40.240
So let's go.
